          "title": "Kein Stich",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Kein Stich is a traditional trick-taking card game using 32-card German or French pack for 4, with 3-6 variants players. It is a compendium game whose name means No Tricks."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Kein Stich is treated as a distinct traditional card game because the source identifies its own player count, pack, rank order, and trick-play objective rather than only listing it as a synonym."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4, with 3-6 variants players use the table arrangement described for Kein Stich."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card German or French pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card German or French pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 32-card German or French pack to 4, with 3-6 variants players according to the local rules before trick play begins."
